0..70 Comment "/// This source gives circle elimination and transport along its loop."
71..74 Comment "///"
75..137 Comment "/// A dependent case carries its point result around the loop."
138..211 Comment "/// A non-dependent case maps the loop to reflexivity without a loop arm."
212..215 Comment "///"
216..285 Comment "/// The checker reads each path type from the words of its operation."
286..347 Comment "/// Transport computes by the family that contains the point."
348..423 Comment "/// In a family of paths, transport composes on the side where the endpoint"
424..501 Comment "/// varies. In a constant family it is the identity. Through a map, it is the"
502..530 Comment "/// map\'s image of the word."
531..534 Comment "///"
535..585 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/circle-base.gandr"
